.TH PROCESS-MEDIA 1 "May 2026" "process-media 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
process-media \- rename and process photos and videos from their EXIF metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B process-media
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B process-media
scans
.I PATH
(a file or directory) for supported photos (JPEG, HEIC) and videos (MP4,
MOV, MKV\(en) reads their EXIF metadata to rename them after the creation
date (\fIYYYYMMDD-HHMMSS\fR), then applies the transformations defined in
a YAML configuration file: rotation, resize, JPEG recompression, metadata
stripping, video re-encoding and thumbnail generation.
.PP
Output flavours are described in named \fIformats\fR, so the same source
collection can be processed in several variants in a single run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-type \fITYPES\fR
Comma-separated media types to process (default: \fBphoto,video\fR).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format \fINAMES\fR
Comma-separated format names from the configuration file. By default all
formats matching the requested types run.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to the YAML configuration file. See
.B FILES
below for the search order.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-max\-threads \fIN\fR
Worker process count (0 = number of CPUs).
.TP
.B \-\-tzoffset \fISECONDS\fR
Seconds added to EXIF timestamps before renaming.
.TP
.B \-k, \-\-keep\-name
Do not rename files from EXIF; keep the original stems.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing target files (default: skip).
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-batch
Non-interactive mode (skip the y/n confirmation prompt).
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
List the planned \fIsource \(-> target\fR mappings without writing anything.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recursive
Scan \fIPATH\fR recursively (descend into subdirectories).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.SH FILES
The configuration file is looked up in this order (first hit wins):
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-config\fR argument.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB$PROCESS_MEDIA_CONFIG\fR environment variable.
.IP \(bu 2
\fIPATH/process-media.yaml\fR (or the parent directory when
.I PATH
is a file).
.IP \(bu 2
\fI./process-media.yaml\fR (current working directory).
.IP \(bu 2
\fI/etc/process-media.yaml\fR.
.PP
An annotated example is shipped in
.I /usr/share/doc/process-media/examples/process-media.yaml.example.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or no input matched the filters).
.TP
.B 1
One or more jobs failed.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error or invalid selection.
.TP
.B 3
A required external tool (ffmpeg, exiftool\(en) is missing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROCESS_MEDIA_CONFIG
Overrides the default search path for the YAML configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR exiftool (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR jpeginfo (1).
